  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0ccf77f6",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a yellow origami brain with the text 'when you have an 80 point iq but it's the highest in your village.' The overall intent is to humorously highlight the relatable experience of having above-average intelligence in a context where it is not recognized or valued, such as a small community. The meme uses the visual metaphor of a brain to represent intelligence, and the juxtaposition of the low IQ score with the high status within a village creates a comedic effect. While not explicitly targeting any specific group, it may unintentionally reinforce ableist stereotypes by mocking intellectual ability, which falls under the 'Harmful' category as it could potentially diminish the value of intelligence or make individuals feel inadequate. The meme is not abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful, but its humor may be perceived as dismissive of intellectual achievement in certain contexts.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d28773a7"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
